# NB: THESE FIVE USED TO BE WRITTEN WITH A LEADING ./, WHICH gitignore DOES NOT UNDERSTAND: A
# PATTERN CONTAINING A SLASH IS MATCHED FROM THE .gitignore's OWN DIRECTORY, AND NOTHING IS EVER
# NAMED '.'. SO build/ AND THE REST WERE NEVER ACTUALLY IGNORED
